<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch cocoa grind up 1.46 pct yr/yr in Q1.</title>
<headline>Dutch cocoa grind up 1.46 pct yr/yr in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch cocoa grind rose 1.46 percent to 102,338 tonnes in the first quarter this year from 100,866 tonnes in the same period of 1996, the Dutch Cocoa Association (NCV) said on Friday.</p>
<p>Analysts had expected the grind to be flat or even slightly lower, dented by a switch at one processor to cocoa liquor.</p>
<p>In the final quarter of 1996, the grind was up 3.90 percent to 97,273 tonnes, giving a full-year total of 388,412 tonnes, up 9.26 percent on 1995's 355,492 tonnes.</p>
<p>--Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
